From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: allow optical probe off during CPU stop

NPU health failure sets ct_stopping before userspace can withdraw its
optical CPU probes. Rejecting off in that state leaves the saved rows
owned and prevents the RAM loopback module from restoring its state.

Allow off while the probe is registered and its teardown work is live.
Keep set and clear blocked during ct_stopping. The existing CPU stop path
closes IFC locally if needed and restores the owner without firmware work;
an outstanding IFC command retains the shadow for a later off retry.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ct_pon_ifc_cpu.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ct_pon_ifc_cpu.h
@@ -330,10 +330,12 @@ static ssize_t ct_pon_cpu_probe_store(struct device *dev,
 	rtnl_lock();
 	mutex_lock(&flow_offload_mutex);
 	if (!READ_ONCE(ppe->ct_pon_ifc_registered) ||
-	    READ_ONCE(ppe->ct_pon_ifc_work_stopping) || READ_ONCE(ppe->ct_stopping))
+	    READ_ONCE(ppe->ct_pon_ifc_work_stopping))
 		err = -ESHUTDOWN;
 	else if (sysfs_streq(buf, "off"))
 		err = airoha_ct_pon_ifc_cpu_stop(ppe);
+	else if (READ_ONCE(ppe->ct_stopping))
+		err = -ESHUTDOWN;
 	else if (!strcmp(command, "set"))
 		err = airoha_ct_pon_ifc_cpu_set(ppe, slot, service);
 	else
